    <briefdescription>
<para>Concept satisfied when the operands of a comparator can be written and compared. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The operands of the comparators must be written in the report of a failed check, and compared with the operator. A single concept for both conditions selects the comparator, and its negation selects the overload that explains why a call is rejected.</para>
